        <p>COUNTY BOROU(41I OF WARRINGTON.— The SANITARY WORKS COMMITTEE are PREPARED TO RECEIVE TENDERS for the supply of SECOND HAND SUGAR BAGS, 10,000 measuring 38ins. by 281ns. to hold licwts. each, and 2,000 measur- ing 34in8, by 241n5. to hold 1 cwt. each, to be delivered free at Longford Depot at the rate of not less than 1,500 per week, deliveries to commence Ist January 1910. Samples may be seen and all further information obtained from the undersigned. Sample bags to be submitted along with tender, and any bag delivered which is not equal in every respect to sample will be rejected. Tenders, in securely fastened envelopes, endorsed " Tender for Bags," and addressed "The Chairman Sanitary Works Committee, Town Hall, Warrington," to be delivered not later than Monday, 15th November 1909. The lowest or any tender will not necessarily be accepted. R. WILSON, Manager. Longford Depat Warrington, 3, November 1909.</p>
