        <p>T 4 ATCHFORD MUNICIPAL ELECTION. NOVEMBER, IST. 1009. £5 REWARD. The above reward will be paid to anyone giving information that will lead to the conviction of the person or persons, wno set out a false rumour that Mr. Hewitts parents died in the Workhouse gni were buried from there. This shameless statement has caused Mr Hewitt and family much pain and was the main cause of the great majority of votes recorded against him on Monday last. J. WOODS, 111, Winwick-road. WARD SECRETARY to Mn. HEWITT. TO THE ELECTORS OF sr. AUSTIN'S WARD LADIES AND GENTLEMEN, I beg to thank you sincerely for the confidence you have placed in me, and for the way you have shown your approval of the work I have undertaken on behalf of the Ratepayers by returning me unopposed. I can assure you I shall continue to do my utmost in the interests of the Ward and the Town generally. Yours obediently, T. H. ASHCR OFT. 135, Sankey-street, Warrington.</p>
