        <p>ELECTORS OF TOWN HALL WARD. LADIES A:.,M GENTLEMEN, Allow me to express my thanks to those Independent voters who came forward and, unsolicited by personal canvas or authorised agents, recorded their votes in my favour on November Ist. lam perfectly satisfied with the result, which was better than expected when one considers the many influences at work against me and the untruthful statements circulated by some of the workers. The allegation that I had been kicked out of the Conservative Association and had sought to become a member of the Liberal Club. and had been rejected by the Liberals, being one of many false statements uttered. Again thanking you, I am, Yours sincerely, JOHN LORD. 12S, Bridge St., Warrington.</p>
