        <p>FaiDAN.—Before the Mayor and other magistrates. Two MONTHS' FOR ASSAULT.—CharIes Campbell of Wainwright's-yard, was sent to gaol for two months' for assault log his wife Ellen Campbell, on Wednesday night. Complainant said defendant went home, he kicked her several times and dragged her off the chair by the hair of her bead. A separation was also granted allowing complainant Bs. per week. FALSE STATEMENT FOR RELIEF.—CIara Shirley, a married woman, was fined 10s. for making a f&lt;tlse state- ment to obtain relief on the 13th October. Defendant told the relieving officer a story and was granted ss. On inqciries being made it was found that her husband was earning on an average the sum of 275, weekly dur- ing the time they were receiving relief.</p>
